# Edit kind

Paths below are relative to the repository root. Read `AGENTS.md` and `.github/agent-context.md` for project conventions. Task modes and delivery authority belong to `packages/ae/corpus/agents/engineer.agent.md`; `docs/adaptive-engineering.md` explains the current contract.

For a write, run the checkout's CLI with `node packages/ae/bin/ae.mjs orient --read --context-version 2` before editing. Use the accepted plan and successful implement gate, then `node packages/ae/bin/ae.mjs verify` with the selected plan and base after review. A globally installed CLI is optional.

Read the relevant source below when the edit needs it. Keep each skill's procedure in its existing file.

| Artifact of this edit | Repository source |
| --- | --- |
| Sketch of a change that is not already the local pattern | `packages/ae/corpus/skills/architect/SKILL.md` |
| New or changed skill, agent, instruction, check, reference, or solution | `packages/ae/corpus/skills/create-primitive/SKILL.md` |
| Judgment of a diff | `packages/ae/corpus/skills/code-review/SKILL.md` |
| Behavior change that extends an existing pattern | `AGENTS.md` |
| Explanation of current behavior or a past decision | `AGENTS.md` |
| Wording change in shipped guidance or documentation | `AGENTS.md` |

Behavior edits follow the repository's failing-regression, minimal-fix, cleanup convention. Explanations use inspected source and Git history, cite the relevant paths or commits, and identify unknown intent. Wording follows the existing artifact's conventions and removes repetition. Editor-only routing stays outside the shipped corpus.
